  "sections": [
    {
      "sectionId": "section-introduction",
      "heading": "Introduction",
      "sourceAnchor": "introduction",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-introduction-1",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Shadow Touched provides a +1 increase to any mental ability score, making this an easy choice for any spellcasting class, but the spellcasting options simply aren’t as universally appealing as "
            },
            {
              "type": "link",
              "text": "Fey Touched",
              "href": "https://rpgbot.net/dnd5/characters/feats/fey-touched/"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": ". First, Invisibility is a powerful but not universally useful spell. While any adventurer can use Misty Step to great effect, Invisibility isn’t always helpful if you’re stomping around in full plate. Similarly, the 1st-level spell options number less than half as many as the options for Fey Touched, and there are few that are truly appealing."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-introduction-2",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "If you are eyeing Shadow Touched, first ask yourself: How is taking this feat better than playing a Glasya Tiefling or a Pallid Elf? If you don’t have a good answer to that question, skip the feat and consider changing races."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-introduction-3",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "For more information about spellcasting feats, including ratings of the various feats, see our "
            },
            {
              "type": "link",
              "text": "Spellcasting Feats Guide",
              "href": "https://rpgbot.net/dnd5/characters/feats/spellcasting-feats/"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
