    {
      "sectionId": "section-disclaimer",
      "heading": "Understanding RPGBOT’s Rating System",
      "sourceAnchor": "disclaimer",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-disclaimer-1",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "RPGBOT uses a color coding scheme which is simple to understand and easy to read at a glance. This system is designed to help players make informed decisions for their dnd character builds."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-disclaimer-2",
          "type": "list",
          "ordered": false,
          "items": [
            [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Red"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": ": Bad, useless options, or options which\n\t\tare extremely situational. Nearly never useful."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Orange"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": ": OK options, or useful options\n\t\tthat only apply in rare circumstances. Useful sometimes."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Green"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": ": Good options. Useful often."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Blue"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": ": Fantastic options, often essential\n\t\tto the function of your character. Useful very frequently."
              }
            ]
          ],
          "depths": [
            0,
            0,
            0,
            0
          ],
          "itemKinds": [
            "unordered",
            "unordered",
            "unordered",
            "unordered"
          ]
        },
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-disclaimer-3",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "The advice offered below is based on the current "
            },
            {
              "type": "link",
              "text": "State of the 2014 DnD 5e Character Optimization Meta",
              "href": "https://rpgbot.net/dnd5/characters/state-of-the-meta/"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": " as of when the article was last updated. Keep in mind that the state of the meta periodically changes as new source materials are released, and the article will be updated accordingly as time allows."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-disclaimer-4",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "We will not include 3rd-party content, Unearthed Arcnaa content, or homebrew in guides for official content because we can’t assume that your game will allow them."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "sectionId": "section-shadow-touched-spells",
      "heading": "Shadow Touched 1st-Level Spell Options",
      "sourceAnchor": "shadow-touched-spells",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-shadow-touched-spells-1",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "For a full list of available spell options and spell descriptions, see\n\t"
            },
            {
              "type": "link",
              "text": "DnDBeyond",
              "href": "https://www.dndbeyond.com/spells?filter-class=0&filter-search=&filter-level=1&filter-school=8&filter-school=9&filter-verbal=&filter-somatic=&filter-material=&filter-concentration=&filter-ritual=&filter-sub-class="
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-shadow-touched-spells-2",
          "type": "list",
          "ordered": false,
          "items": [
            [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Cause Fear"
              },
              {
                "type": "link",
                "text": "XGtE",
                "href": "https://rpgbot.net/dnd5/abbreviations/"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": ": Frightened is a good debuff at any level, but you can find better uses\n\t\tfor your Concentration and immunity to fear is common."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Color spray"
              },
              {
                "type": "link",
                "text": "PHB",
                "href": "https://rpgbot.net/dnd5/abbreviations/"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": ": Doesn’t stay relevant as you level."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Disguise Self"
              },
              {
                "type": "link",
                "text": "PHB",
                "href": "https://rpgbot.net/dnd5/abbreviations/"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": ": Consider playing a changeling or a race which can cast Disguise Self as\n\t\tan innate spell, or get proficiency in disguise kits."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Distort Value"
              },
              {
                "type": "link",
                "text": "AI",
                "href": "https://rpgbot.net/dnd5/abbreviations/"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": ": An amusing but situational novelty."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "False Life"
              },
              {
                "type": "link",
                "text": "PHB",
                "href": "https://rpgbot.net/dnd5/abbreviations/"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": ": A good way to improve your durability, but if this is the reason you’re\n\t\there you might be better served by the Tough feat. You’ll also mitigate more\n\t\ttotal damage as you level with Absorb Elements or Shield since False Life\n\t\twon’t scale, but the damage that you take will."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Illusory Script"
              },
              {
                "type": "link",
                "text": "PHB",
                "href": "https://rpgbot.net/dnd5/abbreviations/"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": ": Take Ritual Caster instead."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Inflict Wounds"
              },
              {
                "type": "link",
                "text": "PHB",
                "href": "https://rpgbot.net/dnd5/abbreviations/"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": ": The damage scales reasonably well with spell level, so if you have spell\n\t\tslots to spend to cast this again it may be worthwhile."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Ray of Sickness"
              },
              {
                "type": "link",
                "text": "PHB",
                "href": "https://rpgbot.net/dnd5/abbreviations/"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": ": Generally just not a great spell. Little damage, short duration, a\n\t\tcommonly-resisted status condition, and it’s all on a Constitution save."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Silent Image"
              },
              {
                "type": "link",
                "text": "PHB",
                "href": "https://rpgbot.net/dnd5/abbreviations/"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": ": Illusions are a ton of fun, but unless you really want Invisibility from\n\t\tShadow Touched I would consider Magic Initiate first so that you can also\n\t\tlearn Minor Illusion."
              }
            ]
          ],
          "depths": [
            0,
            0,
            0,
            0,
            0,
            0,
            0,
